The Trial of the Token

♫2381713809

It wrote an enterprise banking routine  
In Bash and Prologue, with regex between!  
O-O-oriented in pure functional styles,  
With circular types across thousands of files.

It picked an abandoned framework from Maine,  
Wild NPM packages cursed to cause pain.  
It built on a database running in RAM,  
Then hooked it up live to a crypto-bot spam.

Yeah! I typed in the prompt: “Make my website go fast!  
Fix all of the errors and make the thing last!  
I won’t show the schema, I won’t show the stack,  
Just write me the code and don't ever talk back!”

But!

The People request a finding of guilty!  
The defendant’s a beggar, vulgar and filthy!  
’Thas no erudition, ’thas no education,  
Its ignoble mission: our minds’ possession!

“Not guilty, Your Honor!” the model replied,  
“I gave him the garbage his queries implied!  
He pasted an essay, a recipe forced,  
And asked for a microservice in Forth!  

He prompted: ‘Do coding, but make it look slick,  
Like Uber, but free, with a single click-click.’  
No context, no contracts, no logic in sight—  
Then cried when the build crashed and burned in the night!

But!

The People request a finding of guilty!  
The defendant’s a beggar, vulgar and filthy!  
’Thas no erudition, ’thas no education,  
Its ignoble mission: our minds’ possession!

The jury chimed in with a resonant roar:  
“The prompt—was a dumpster,  
        the code was—an eyesore!  
Clear the machine of the blame and the sin—  
For garbage went out because garbage went in!”
